  "body": "History.pushState has failure modes for the document not being fully active (steps 2 and 3 of https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/history.html#dom-history-pushstate). However, when history.pushState is called during an unload event, the document may still be fully active, but navigation may not be possible at that point. The history delta traversal algorithm specifically states that an exit should happen if traversal is tried during an unload (step 4 of https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/history.html#traverse-the-history-by-a-delta, though that's covering more ground than the unload event specifically), so it'd be nice to clarify this for other state manipulations too.\r\n\r\nRelevant firefox bug: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1450164",
